WEBVTT

00:01.410 --> 00:05.540
The Survey Corps left to 
find a route to Zhiganshina,

00:06.020 --> 00:09.080
but encountered an 
intelligent Female Titan.

00:16.840 --> 00:19.900
As soldiers died, one after the next,

00:19.900 --> 00:23.210
they headed into a 
forest of giant trees,

00:23.210 --> 00:25.370
none of them knowing why.

00:25.960 --> 00:29.510
If Squad Levi doesn't 
defeat it, who will?

00:31.540 --> 00:32.760
Another one's dead...

00:33.720 --> 00:35.750
And maybe we could've saved him!

00:37.060 --> 00:37.960
Choose.

00:38.610 --> 00:40.010
Believe in yourself.

00:40.600 --> 00:44.270
Or believe in the Survey Corps and me.

00:47.070 --> 00:48.480
I'll go forward!

00:55.130 --> 00:56.780
Fire!

01:05.180 --> 01:06.080
He can't intend

01:06.970 --> 01:09.670
to take that Titan alive?

01:10.160 --> 01:12.170
Well, Eren? See that?

01:12.170 --> 01:14.050
We caught that Titan!

01:14.050 --> 01:16.350
This is the power of the Survey Corps!

01:16.350 --> 01:18.180
Don't underestimate us, fool.

01:18.180 --> 01:19.930
Well? Do you get it now?

01:21.370 --> 01:22.250
Yes!

01:25.690 --> 01:27.390
Looks like it's stopped moving...

01:28.220 --> 01:29.650
We can't lower our guard.

01:30.330 --> 01:33.810
But you did well, leading it here.

01:34.480 --> 01:39.510
Men in the rearguard squads died 
buying us the time we needed.

01:40.390 --> 01:42.450
We couldn't have done it without them.

01:42.810 --> 01:43.770
Is that so?

01:44.320 --> 01:45.410
It is.

01:46.730 --> 01:51.340
Thanks to them, we'll be able 
to see who's inside this thing.

01:52.980 --> 01:56.080
I hope they haven't pissed themselves...

03:30.980 --> 03:35.980
Erwin Smith 
57th Expedition Beyond the Walls (4)

03:42.920 --> 03:43.990
An Aberrant?

03:44.390 --> 03:47.160
Or is it like the Colossal Titan?

03:49.180 --> 03:50.940
Did Commander Erwin...

03:50.940 --> 03:53.570
Hey, snap out of it!

03:53.570 --> 03:55.820
Eren, think later.

03:55.820 --> 03:57.610
We need to get farther in and stand by!

03:58.110 --> 03:58.750
Right!

04:05.240 --> 04:06.100
Wait, Levi...

04:06.950 --> 04:08.370
An eye for an eye.

04:08.920 --> 04:11.680
Waves 2 and 3, fire!

04:12.500 --> 04:14.420
Fire the spare rounds!

04:32.640 --> 04:35.170
Um, it's climbing up...

04:35.170 --> 04:36.440
Yeah.

04:36.440 --> 04:39.800
If it gets this far, I'll 
move out of the way.

04:40.530 --> 04:43.540
But I don't think it will be long before

04:43.540 --> 04:45.780
they issue withdrawal orders.

04:45.780 --> 04:48.700
Does that have something 
to do with the explosions

04:48.700 --> 04:50.870
we've been hearing deep within the forest?

04:50.870 --> 04:51.870
I don't know.

04:55.020 --> 04:58.240
Mikasa, what do you think that sound is?

04:58.820 --> 05:01.410
Are they firing cannons in the forest?

05:04.560 --> 05:07.540
It didn't seem like they'd 
brought cannons, though.

05:08.120 --> 05:10.130
It's really loud back there.

05:10.880 --> 05:12.240
Hey, Bertolt...

05:12.500 --> 05:14.840
Do you know where Krista went?

05:14.840 --> 05:16.870
Sorry, I don't know.

05:17.300 --> 05:19.270
I have no idea what's going on.

05:19.550 --> 05:21.640
What am I doing and why?

05:21.970 --> 05:23.090
I want to go home.

05:26.100 --> 05:27.690
We're going to shift position, Armin.

05:27.690 --> 05:28.390
Okay.

05:35.750 --> 05:38.190
They've started to figure it out.

05:38.570 --> 05:41.070
They seem to keep getting better 
and better at climbing.

05:41.070 --> 05:44.570
That means, scary as it 
sounds, they can learn.

05:44.700 --> 05:46.660
Although some are better 
than others, I'm sure.

05:47.370 --> 05:48.570
Armin...

05:48.790 --> 05:51.330
Sounds like something is going 
on deeper in the forest.

05:51.630 --> 05:53.630
I think I have some idea what.

05:54.590 --> 05:59.010
They lured that Female Titan all the 
way here in order to capture it.

06:00.460 --> 06:01.960
More precisely...

06:02.720 --> 06:05.310
To capture whoever is inside of it.

06:06.270 --> 06:07.930
That was Commander Erwin's goal...

06:09.440 --> 06:11.480
That was his plan from the very start!

06:11.480 --> 06:12.940
Right?

06:13.650 --> 06:16.500
I can see why he wouldn't 
have told the new troops.

06:16.860 --> 06:18.350
But why wouldn't he tell you

06:18.610 --> 06:20.990
when you've all been with the 
Survey Corps for so long?

06:20.990 --> 06:22.160
Shut up!

06:22.160 --> 06:26.330
Are you saying the Commander 
and the Captain don't trust us?

06:26.870 --> 06:29.870
But that's what this means...

06:29.870 --> 06:32.160
Petra, rip out his teeth!

06:32.160 --> 06:33.900
Swap the front and back teeth 
when you shove 'em back in!

06:33.900 --> 06:35.870
No, Eren's right.

06:36.750 --> 06:41.220
I think there was a reason the 
Commander couldn't trust us.

06:42.220 --> 06:43.220
Like what?

06:43.220 --> 06:46.220
There's only one reason he 
wouldn't trust his fellow soldiers.

06:46.760 --> 06:49.090
There's someone who can become a Titan,

06:49.090 --> 06:52.710
or a spy helping them, 
in the Survey Corps.

06:54.310 --> 06:56.250
You think so, too, right?

06:57.200 --> 06:58.390
It has to be one of us.

07:00.090 --> 07:01.300
Yes, I think so.

07:06.490 --> 07:07.900
A spy?

07:08.150 --> 07:09.620
Is that possible?

07:10.000 --> 07:13.280
At any rate, the Commander is certain.

07:13.540 --> 07:16.790
I'd imagine the only soldiers who 
were told of the plan were those

07:16.790 --> 07:19.130
who've stayed alive for 
the past five years.

07:19.130 --> 07:20.040
I see...

07:20.040 --> 07:21.530
So that's it.

07:21.530 --> 07:23.470
Must be.

07:23.470 --> 07:24.800
Understand, Eren?

07:24.800 --> 07:26.050
That's why.

07:26.350 --> 07:28.890
Yeah, if that's the 
reason, I understand.

07:30.140 --> 07:33.730
He's assuming that five years ago, 
when the first wall fell,

07:33.730 --> 07:35.930
a spy infiltrated our ranks...

07:36.310 --> 07:38.400
And that's how he narrowed 
down the possibilities.

07:39.190 --> 07:42.940
Then, the spy killed Sawney and Bean?

07:43.990 --> 07:48.330
Back then, the Commander 
asked me about that.

07:50.670 --> 07:52.240
What do you see?

07:53.210 --> 07:54.990
What do you think the enemy is?

07:55.670 --> 07:58.000
That's what the question meant?

07:58.000 --> 08:00.250
If we could've answered it,

08:00.420 --> 08:03.170
maybe we could've 
participated in this plan.

08:04.180 --> 08:06.300
I doubt that anyone could've 
back then, though.

08:06.300 --> 08:08.220
I knew.

08:08.220 --> 08:11.140
But I didn't say anything.

08:11.520 --> 08:13.760
Do you know why?

08:14.330 --> 08:15.310
Why?

08:16.150 --> 08:18.440
What, you can't tell?

08:18.810 --> 08:21.600
Well, I shouldn't expect that 
much from the likes of you.

08:21.780 --> 08:25.150
You have yet to reach my level.

08:25.150 --> 08:28.360
Hey, are you copying Captain Levi again?

08:28.620 --> 08:30.450
The Captain wouldn't 
say anything like that.

08:30.450 --> 08:34.620
If this succeeds, I can get closer 
to the truth of this world.

08:35.500 --> 08:42.050
But... Too many died, regardless.

08:46.090 --> 08:48.340
Do you think the Commander was wrong?

08:52.350 --> 08:54.560
I can't say he was right.

08:54.560 --> 08:58.280
If we'd known there was a Titan 
informed of our operations,

08:58.690 --> 09:00.500
we would've dealt with 
this in a different way.

09:01.110 --> 09:03.480
Your team's squad leader and 
the others would've, too.

09:08.210 --> 09:10.390
No, it wasn't wrong.

09:11.080 --> 09:12.690
What wasn't wrong?

09:12.990 --> 09:15.650
How many do you think 
died for no reason?

09:16.410 --> 09:21.090
Jean, after the fact, it's easy to say, 
"We should've done something else."

09:21.090 --> 09:21.910
However,

09:22.640 --> 09:25.120
no one knows how things will turn out.

09:25.120 --> 09:27.920
And even so, you have to make a choice.

09:28.260 --> 09:29.390
You must.

09:30.510 --> 09:32.720
The lives of a hundred 
fellow soldiers...

09:32.720 --> 09:34.770
Or the lives of all the humans 
within the walls...

09:35.640 --> 09:37.260
The Commander made his choice.

09:37.770 --> 09:41.360
He chose to let those hundred die.

09:41.980 --> 09:45.400
Eren, you don't know it yet,

09:45.400 --> 09:47.070
but you will soon.

09:47.650 --> 09:51.650
The reason that Erwin Smith is 
entrusted with humanity's hope,

09:51.650 --> 09:53.190
the Survey Corps.

09:53.830 --> 09:56.790
Just look at how much 
Captain Levi trusts him!

09:56.980 --> 10:00.160
If you live that long...

10:01.630 --> 10:03.660
I haven't lived that long,

10:04.100 --> 10:05.840
but I'm certain of one thing.

10:06.510 --> 10:09.810
If there's anyone who can bring change,

10:09.810 --> 10:13.670
it will be someone willing to 
sacrifice what they care for.

10:14.680 --> 10:17.850
It will be someone who can throw aside

10:17.850 --> 10:20.770
their humanity, in order 
to defeat monsters.

10:22.020 --> 10:24.520
Someone who can't sacrifice anything

10:24.860 --> 10:27.150
can't ever change anything!

10:29.020 --> 10:34.020
<b>Information We Can Share So Far:</b>

10:29.020 --> 10:34.020
<b>Special Target Capture Weapon (1) 
A newly developed weapon the Survey Corps 
created to capture a specific Titan.</b>

10:34.020 --> 10:39.030
<b>Information We Can Share So Far:</b>

10:34.020 --> 10:39.030
<b>Special Target Capture Weapon (2) 
The barrels are loaded with seven steel tubes, 
each of which has coiled wires with arrowheads at both ends.</b>

10:40.110 --> 10:41.650
Fire!

10:45.870 --> 10:47.370
How do you like that?

10:47.370 --> 10:49.830
You won't even be able 
to scratch an itch now.

10:49.830 --> 10:53.290
You won't be able to make a single move. 
Probably for the rest of your life.

10:54.460 --> 10:56.760
They're designed so that the 
more you heal your wounds,

10:56.760 --> 10:59.680
the more immobilized your joints become!

11:02.890 --> 11:06.270
But they still can't draw 
out whoever is inside?

11:06.640 --> 11:09.730
What are Levi and Mike doing?

11:34.710 --> 11:39.710
It can selectively harden its skin 
to protect specific parts of its body?

11:40.220 --> 11:43.430
It's similar to what I've 
heard of the Armored Titan.

11:44.920 --> 11:49.280
If we continue using the Maneuver 
Gear and blades, will it weaken?

11:50.480 --> 11:52.310
We don't have time to find out.

11:52.310 --> 11:53.300
In that case...

11:55.270 --> 11:56.190
Yes, sir?

11:56.190 --> 11:57.320
Prepare the explosives.

11:57.980 --> 11:59.820
Blow off its hands.

11:59.820 --> 12:00.570
Yes, sir...

12:01.300 --> 12:04.320
But there's a chance 
that the amount we carry

12:04.910 --> 12:07.830
has enough firepower to 
also blow up what's inside.

12:07.830 --> 12:11.500
Then set them to amputate the wrists.

12:12.750 --> 12:15.000
Set them all off at once at my signal.

12:15.000 --> 12:15.830
Roger.

12:25.390 --> 12:26.350
Hey...

12:26.800 --> 12:29.040
Why not just come out?

12:29.720 --> 12:32.340
We don't have time to waste.

12:33.060 --> 12:34.020
So...

12:34.020 --> 12:36.240
What do you think will 
happen to you now?

12:37.020 --> 12:41.280
Do you believe you can escape?

12:42.400 --> 12:45.660
I wish you'd consider all the 
trouble we're going through...

12:46.760 --> 12:51.080
As I recall, you killed 
my troops in various ways.

12:51.450 --> 12:53.660
Did you find it fun?

12:55.120 --> 12:56.880
Right now, I'm having fun.

12:57.270 --> 12:59.900
Well, so are you, right?

13:01.090 --> 13:04.430
I think you can understand me.

13:06.970 --> 13:08.140
Oh, right...

13:08.490 --> 13:10.560
I wanted to ask you something.

13:11.850 --> 13:14.690
Is it okay if we cut off 
your hands and legs?

13:15.680 --> 13:17.540
They'll grow back, right?

13:18.050 --> 13:20.480
I'm talking about <i>your </i>
limbs, not the Titan's.

13:21.480 --> 13:24.990
We need you alive, after all...

13:56.740 --> 13:59.730
Well, that was a surprise.

14:01.820 --> 14:03.730
Were those her dying screams?

14:07.000 --> 14:08.420
Erwin, it stinks.

14:08.810 --> 14:09.700
What direction?

14:10.030 --> 14:12.490
Multiple sources, from 
all directions at once.

14:17.620 --> 14:18.960
What's up with them?

14:18.960 --> 14:20.460
They're all running into the forest?

14:20.860 --> 14:22.570
Why did they suddenly start ignoring us?

14:27.300 --> 14:28.180
What?

14:28.800 --> 14:31.600
They're all Aberrants?

14:31.600 --> 14:33.640
It doesn't matter! 
Don't let them through!

14:34.470 --> 14:36.310
Begin combat!

14:38.640 --> 14:40.060
What just happened?

14:40.440 --> 14:41.650
Wait...

14:43.150 --> 14:45.860
I've heard that scream before.

14:46.070 --> 14:47.700
In the forests where I'm from...

14:48.120 --> 14:51.870
It's the cry of a cornered animal 
that has nothing to lose!

14:51.870 --> 14:55.630
I was taught to exercise greater caution 
once a hunt drew to a close!

14:56.200 --> 14:58.080
So be careful?

14:58.080 --> 15:00.420
A hundred times more than usual!

15:00.420 --> 15:02.630
If you underestimate 
the forest, you'll die!

15:03.090 --> 15:05.710
I grew up in the mountains, too.

15:05.710 --> 15:08.090
Someone who grew crops 
wouldn't understand!

15:08.220 --> 15:08.920
I see.

15:10.130 --> 15:13.140
It's true that Sasha's 
intuition is usually good.

15:13.600 --> 15:16.600
Especially when she predicts 
things are going sour.

15:17.600 --> 15:21.690
Armin thought Eren would be in 
the center, toward the rear...

15:27.740 --> 15:29.150
Ready those explosives, now!

15:30.030 --> 15:31.160
Erwin...

15:31.160 --> 15:32.660
The first wave will come from the east.

15:32.660 --> 15:33.570
They're almost here.

15:35.450 --> 15:37.490
Cart guard team, intercept!

15:44.590 --> 15:45.670
They ignored us?

15:45.670 --> 15:46.800
Are they Aberrants?

15:47.680 --> 15:49.130
Three are breaking through!

15:50.340 --> 15:51.900
Captain Levi!

15:51.900 --> 15:55.600
You just did something, 
didn't you, bitch?

16:06.480 --> 16:08.550
So they're after the Female Titan?

16:11.110 --> 16:13.860
Titans from all directions!

16:14.450 --> 16:16.280
All men, engage.

16:16.780 --> 16:19.290
Defend the Female Titan, 
even if it means your lives!

16:35.050 --> 16:36.010
It's no use!

16:49.980 --> 16:51.530
Retreat, men!

16:53.610 --> 16:55.360
Back into formation!

16:56.530 --> 16:58.530
Return to Karanes!

17:16.930 --> 17:18.140
We've been had.

17:19.760 --> 17:21.600
Just look at you.

17:22.220 --> 17:23.810
Don't tell me...

17:23.810 --> 17:24.980
The enemy

17:25.320 --> 17:28.440
was willing to sacrifice everything.

17:29.860 --> 17:33.240
I didn't expect the enemy to destroy 
itself along with the evidence

17:33.240 --> 17:35.150
by making Titans devour itself.

17:37.160 --> 17:40.780
All our talk at the court martial, 
and this is what happens.

17:41.290 --> 17:43.300
If we return empty-handed, who knows

17:43.300 --> 17:45.300

what will happen to Eren or us.

17:45.960 --> 17:47.650
We can think about that after we return.

17:48.330 --> 17:52.130
Our priority now is getting home 
without additional casualties.

17:53.210 --> 17:54.280
For now...

17:56.220 --> 17:58.200
The steam from the corpse is limiting visibility.

17:58.840 --> 18:01.430
It could interfere with our signal 
flare message relay system.

18:07.290 --> 18:08.770
I'll call my team.

18:09.560 --> 18:10.400
Wait, Levi...

18:11.630 --> 18:13.420
Refill your gas and blades.

18:13.690 --> 18:15.170
There isn't time.

18:15.170 --> 18:16.780
I think I have plenty.

18:16.780 --> 18:17.680
Why?

18:18.110 --> 18:19.240
That's an order.

18:19.820 --> 18:21.030
Follow it.

18:21.890 --> 18:23.660
Roger, Erwin.

18:25.120 --> 18:27.170
I trust your decision.

18:40.890 --> 18:41.930
We're retreating.

18:42.390 --> 18:43.760
Everyone, retreat.

18:44.260 --> 18:45.720
Get back on your horse, and retreat.

18:45.720 --> 18:46.600
Right!

18:47.060 --> 18:49.610
What? It's already over?

18:52.690 --> 18:54.730
We can go home! All right!

18:55.860 --> 18:57.440
What's going on?

18:58.240 --> 18:59.280
Where's Eren?

19:00.990 --> 19:02.530
Looks like it's over.

19:03.290 --> 19:05.550
Back to the horses! Prepare to retreat!

19:06.120 --> 19:07.250
You heard the man...

19:07.250 --> 19:11.670
Let's go see what the 
bastard inside looks like.

19:14.040 --> 19:16.420
Will we really find out who it is?

19:16.420 --> 19:17.840
It's thanks to you.

19:18.310 --> 19:19.730
I didn't really do anything.

19:20.180 --> 19:22.180
You had faith in us.

19:22.890 --> 19:27.020
This is the result of your choice 
to trust us back then.

19:27.020 --> 19:30.650
Making the right choice isn't easy.

19:31.560 --> 19:34.940
Hey, don't spoil him, Petra...

19:35.190 --> 19:37.190
What did he do, anyway?

19:37.190 --> 19:40.560
He was pathetic. He just kept whining.

19:40.560 --> 19:44.200
Well, coming back alive on your 
first excursion is pretty good.

19:44.200 --> 19:47.410
But it doesn't count 
until the mission's over.

19:48.000 --> 19:52.250
Listen, kiddo, the expedition lasts 
until you're at home in bed...

19:52.250 --> 19:54.750
Jeez, I know that!

19:57.380 --> 19:58.960
Oluo! Petra!

19:58.960 --> 20:02.130
You guys pissed your pants and 
cried on your first mission.

20:02.470 --> 20:03.640
You're all grown up now!

20:05.390 --> 20:06.510
Don't say that!

20:06.510 --> 20:09.220
What if he stops respecting me?!

20:09.600 --> 20:10.520
It's true?

20:10.520 --> 20:11.770
It sure is.

20:11.770 --> 20:14.230
And I didn't, by the way, Eren.

20:14.230 --> 20:15.270
Idiot!

20:15.270 --> 20:18.040
I've killed more of them than you!

20:18.040 --> 20:19.570
More of them than you, idiot!

20:19.570 --> 20:22.570
Kill count isn't all 
that makes a soldier.

20:22.570 --> 20:24.110
Shut up, idiot!

20:24.110 --> 20:24.870
Petra...

20:25.030 --> 20:26.990
Does that mean you sprayed 
it everywhere while mid-air?

20:26.990 --> 20:28.290
Shut up!

20:28.290 --> 20:30.080
Do you think you're on a picnic?

20:30.080 --> 20:31.940
We're outside the walls!

20:31.940 --> 20:34.310
I didn't piss my pants, either, Eren.

20:44.670 --> 20:47.890
Oh, I'm sure that's the 
signal from Captain Levi.

20:48.390 --> 20:49.890
We'll rendezvous with the Captain!

20:49.890 --> 20:51.730
Cut the chatter till we get back.

21:12.600 --> 21:13.540
Erwin...

21:14.040 --> 21:16.040
Why did you order Levi to resupply?

21:16.040 --> 21:17.130
There's no time to waste.

21:17.880 --> 21:19.340
The Female Titan was eaten.

21:19.750 --> 21:22.640
But did you see the 
person inside get eaten?

21:23.300 --> 21:24.300
I didn't.

21:25.550 --> 21:26.590
You can't mean...

21:26.590 --> 21:27.300
Yes...

21:27.590 --> 21:30.060
If your original hypothesis was correct,

21:30.060 --> 21:34.230
and they can still move to a degree 
after regaining human form...

21:35.190 --> 21:39.300
And if they'd equipped 
Maneuver Gear in advance...

21:40.870 --> 21:45.290
The one within the Female Titan 
is wearing our uniform right now.

21:46.530 --> 21:47.900
Captain Levi?

21:48.950 --> 21:50.630
No, it's not!

21:50.630 --> 21:51.200
Who are you?!

22:00.550 --> 22:01.670
G-Gunther!

22:01.670 --> 22:03.420
What? Why?

22:04.480 --> 22:05.510
Gunther!

22:14.260 --> 22:18.020
The enemy is now camouflaged 
as one of our men.

23:53.370 --> 23:55.430
The capture operation has failed.

23:56.030 --> 23:59.280
The Female Titan appears 
before Eren once more.

23:59.680 --> 24:01.830
What stands between it and its target

24:01.830 --> 24:04.210
are the master Titan killers,

24:04.210 --> 24:06.280
the Special Ops Squad.

24:04.220 --> 24:07.680
Crushing Blow 
 57th Expedition Beyond the Walls (5)
